menu "DeskBuddy"

    config DESKBUDDY_STAGE_PERCENT
        int "Character stage width (% of the screen)"
        range 40 100
        default 65
        help
            The rest of the width is reserved for the touchscreen control panel. The boundary is rounded to
            32 pixels so stage and panel redraws never share a dirty-rectangle column.

    config DESKBUDDY_PANEL_LEFT
        bool "Put the control-panel area on the left"
        default n

    config DESKBUDDY_BACKLIGHT_PERCENT
        int "Backlight brightness (%)"
        range 3 100
        default 80

    config DESKBUDDY_TIMEZONE
        string "Time zone (POSIX TZ string)"
        default "CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3"
        help
            Local time zone for the Office Mode clock, including daylight saving rules. The default is
            Central European Time (Amsterdam, Brussels, Berlin). The clock itself is kept in UTC.

    config DESKBUDDY_PERF_LOG_S
        int "Performance log interval in seconds (0 = off)"
        range 0 3600
        default 5

    config DESKBUDDY_DEMO_POKE_S
        int "Poke the character automatically every N seconds (0 = off)"
        range 0 3600
        default 0
        help
            Runs the reaction animations without touching the screen, for hands-off measurements.

    config DESKBUDDY_DEMO_MONSTER_S
        int "Start the Monster Energy animation automatically every N seconds (0 = off)"
        range 0 3600
        default 0
        help
            Plays the Monster charging sequence without touching the screen, for hands-off measurements.
            Normally it is started by tapping the Monster can in the control panel.

    config DESKBUDDY_DEMO_OFFICE_S
        int "Toggle Office Mode automatically every N seconds (0 = off)"
        range 0 3600
        default 0
        help
            Switches between DeskBuddy and the Office Mode clock without touching the screen, for hands-off
            tests of the scene switch. Normally it is toggled with the moon button and a tap on the clock.

    config DESKBUDDY_GFX_VERIFY
        bool "Verify every presented frame against a full redraw (debug, slow)"
        default n
        help
            After each incremental redraw, the whole scene is also drawn into a scratch PSRAM buffer and compared
            with the frame about to be shown. Any difference means a missed dirty region. Costs 1.2 MB of PSRAM and
            roughly 100 ms per frame, so animation runs slower while enabled.

endmenu
